ees":"64500","description":"The Brink's Company operates as a global leader in secure logistics, cash management, and comprehensive security services, with operations spanning North America, Latin America, Europe, and other international markets. A core offering is the secure transportation of high-value assets. This encompasses armored vehicle services for cash-in-transit, as well as the specialized movement of diamonds, jewelry, precious metals, securities, banknotes, currency, sophisticated electronics, and pharmaceuticals. The company delivers a full spectrum of automated teller machine (ATM) services. These range from cash replenishment, predictive forecasting, and optimization to remote monitoring, service call dispatch, transaction processing, installation, and multi-level maintenance, all supported by essential network infrastructure. Further extending its cash services, Brink's offers vault outsourcing and detailed money processing solutions, including cashier balancing, counterfeit detection, account consolidation, electronic reporting, check imaging, and reconciliation. They also handle the deployment and servicing of intelligent safes and their associated control devices. Technological solutions feature web-based applications for functions such as online cash tracking and streamlined cash inventory management. Brink's designs, installs, and maintains a broad array of physical security systems. This includes alarms, motion detectors, closed-circuit television (CCTV) with digital video recorders (DVRs), and advanced access control systems employing card readers, biometric scanners, electronic locks, and turnstiles. Additionally, they provide monitoring services and on-site guarding to secure diverse environments like airports, corporate offices, warehouses, retail establishments, and public venues. The company also facilitates bill payment and collection services, alongside offering prepaid and corporate debit cards. Their extensive client base includes banks, financial institutions, retailers, government agencies, mints, jewelers, and various other commercial operations. Founded in 1859, The Brink's Company is headquartered in Richmond, Virginia. It operated as The Pittston Company until its rebranding to The Brink's Company in May 2003.","description_en":"The Brink's Company operates as a global leader in secure logistics, cash management, and comprehensive security services, with operations spanning North America, Latin America, Europe, and other international markets. A core offering is the secure transportation of high-value assets. This encompasses armored vehicle services for cash-in-transit, as well as the specialized movement of diamonds, jewelry, precious metals, securities, banknotes, currency, sophisticated electronics, and pharmaceuticals. The company delivers a full spectrum of automated teller machine (ATM) services. These range from cash replenishment, predictive forecasting, and optimization to remote monitoring, service call dispatch, transaction processing, installation, and multi-level maintenance, all supported by essential network infrastructure. Further extending its cash services, Brink's offers vault outsourcing and detailed money processing solutions, including cashier balancing, counterfeit detection, account consolidation, electronic reporting, check imaging, and reconciliation. They also handle the deployment and servicing of intelligent safes and their associated control devices. Technological solutions feature web-based applications for functions such as online cash tracking and streamlined cash inventory management. Brink's designs, installs, and maintains a broad array of physical security systems. This includes alarms, motion detectors, closed-circuit television (CCTV) with digital video recorders (DVRs), and advanced access control systems employing card readers, biometric scanners, electronic locks, and turnstiles. Additionally, they provide monitoring services and on-site guarding to secure diverse environments like airports, corporate offices, warehouses, retail establishments, and public venues. The company also facilitates bill payment and collection services, alongside offering prepaid and corporate debit cards. Their extensive client base includes banks, financial institutions, retailers, government agencies, mints, jewelers, and various other commercial operations. Founded in 1859, The Brink's Company is headquartered in Richmond, Virginia. It operated as The Pittston Company until its rebranding to The Brink's Company in May 2003.","description_zh":"The Brink's Company（美股代碼：BCO）為 Industrials 領域之重要企業，專注於 Security & Protection Services 業務，具備清晰之商業壁壘與現金流創造能力。","address":"1801 Bayberry Court","city":"Richmond","state":"VA","zip":"23226-8100","country":"US","phone":"804 289 9600","full_address":"1801 Bayberry Court, Richmond, VA 23226-8100, US","range_52w":"91.05-136.37","year_high":136.37,"year_low":91.05,"all_time_high":0,"all_time_low":91.05,"inst_ownership_pct":null,"insider_ownership_pct":null,"top_holders":[],"insider_trades":[{"date":"2026-11-03","name":"Button Adrian","title":"officer: EVP","is_buy":null,"action":"A-Award","shares":52,"price":0,"total_val":0},{"date":"2026-11-03","name":"Galloway Elizabeth A","title":"officer: EVP and CHRO","is_buy":null,"action":"A-Award","shares":42,"price":0,"total_val":0},{"date":"2026-11-03","name":"Eubanks Richard M.","title":"director, officer: President and CEO","is_buy":null,"action":"A-Award","shares":116,"price":0,"total_val":0},{"date":"2026-11-03","name":"Cook Kristen Williams","title":"officer: EVP & CLO","is_buy":null,"action":"A-Award","shares":67,"price":0,"total_val":0},{"date":"2026-11-03","name":"Peschard Mijares Guillermo Eduardo","title":"officer: EVP","is_buy":null,"action":"A-Award","shares":55,"price":0,"total_val":0},{"date":"2026-11-03","name":"McMaken Kurt B","title":"officer: EVP, Chief Financial Officer","is_buy":null,"action":"A-Award","shares":65,"price":0,"total_val"